1
00:03:17,142 --> 00:03:23,142
The world was in a mess... but their hair was perfect!!

2
00:06:34,285 --> 00:06:40,285
Hairspray is a comedy, music, romance film directed by John Waters.

3
00:09:51,428 --> 00:09:57,428
'Pleasantly plump' teenager Tracy Turnblad achieves her dream of
becoming a regular on the Corny Collins Dance Show.

4
00:13:08,571 --> 00:13:14,571
Now a teen hero, she starts using her fame to speak out for the
causes she believes in, most of all integration.

5
00:16:25,714 --> 00:16:31,714
In doing so, she earns the wrath of the show's former star, Amber Von
Tussle, as well as Amber's manipulative, pro-segregation parents.

6
00:19:42,857 --> 00:19:48,857
The rivalry comes to a head as Amber and Tracy vie
for the title of Miss Auto Show 1963.

7
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Tracy Turnblad, played by Ricki Lake.

8
00:26:17,142 --> 00:26:23,142
Edna Turnblad / Arvin Hodgepile, played by Divine.

9
00:29:34,285 --> 00:29:40,285
Velma Von Tussle, played by Debbie Harry.

10
00:32:51,428 --> 00:32:57,428
Amber von Tussle, played by Vitamin C.

11
00:36:08,571 --> 00:36:14,571
Franklin von Tussle, played by Sonny Bono.

12
00:39:25,714 --> 00:39:31,714
Penny Pingleton, played by Leslie Ann Powers.

13
00:42:42,857 --> 00:42:48,857
Hairspray is a 1988 American musical comedy film written and directed by John Waters, starring Sonny Bono, Ruth Brown, Divine,
Debbie Harry, Ricki Lake in her film debut, and Jerry Stiller, with special appearances by Ric Ocasek and Pia Zadora.

14
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Hairspray was a dramatic departure from Waters's earlier
works, with a much broader intended audience.

15
00:49:17,142 --> 00:49:23,142
Hairspray's PG is the least restrictive rating a Waters film has
received; most of his previous films were rated X by the MPAA.

16
00:52:34,285 --> 00:52:40,285
Set in 1962 Baltimore, Maryland, the film revolves around self-proclaimed "pleasantly plump" teenager Tracy
Turnblad as she pursues stardom as a dancer on a local TV show and rallies against racial segregation.

17
00:55:51,428 --> 00:55:57,428
Hairspray was a moderate success upon its initial
theatrical release, earning $8 million.

18
00:59:08,571 --> 00:59:14,571
However, it managed to attract a larger audience
on home video in the early 1990s.

19
01:02:25,714 --> 01:02:31,714
The film received critical acclaim and ranks at No.

20
01:05:42,857 --> 01:05:48,857
444 on Empire magazine's 2008 list of the 500 greatest films of all time.

21
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
This is Divine's final film released during his lifetime.

22
01:12:17,142 --> 01:12:23,142
He died three weeks after its release.

23
01:15:34,285 --> 01:15:40,285
In 2002, the film was adapted into a Broadway musical of the same name,
which won eight Tony Awards, including Best Musical in 2003.

24
01:18:51,428 --> 01:18:57,428
A second film version of Hairspray, an adaptation of the stage musical, was also released by New
Line Cinema in 2007, which included many changes of scripted items from the original.

25
01:22:08,571 --> 01:22:14,571
In 2022, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

26
01:25:25,714 --> 01:25:31,714
The film explores themes of bomb, baltimore, usa,
civil rights, romcom, racial segregation.

27
01:28:42,857 --> 01:28:48,857
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
